&quot;The impact on journalism has been clear. Just within the past week, we have seen over 1,000 planned layoffs at Gannett, BuzzFeed and HuffPost&quot;<p>I had never considered the click-bait outlet &quot;HuffPost&quot; as &quot;quality journalism&quot;.<p>&quot;We can start with the fact that “free” isn’t a good business model for quality journalism.&quot;
Well, paid journalism is not a guarantee either:
<a href="http:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.spiegel.de&#x2F;international&#x2F;zeitgeist&#x2F;claas-relotius-reporter-forgery-scandal-a-1244755.html" rel="nofollow">http:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.spiegel.de&#x2F;international&#x2F;zeitgeist&#x2F;claas-relotius...</a><p>Stopped reading after this. Whining does not suit the NYT well. It is an outstanding newspaper and has basically, also thanks to the internet, a world wide audience. It is better prepared to the changing business model as most other newspapers. Whining here about google and facebook is rent seeking.
